abstract: >-
  FrameAssembly is a domain-specific language (DSL) and optimizing compiler written in Rust
  that compiles declarative network packet specifications (.fasm) into deterministic,
  wire-valid PCAPNG (.pcap) packet captures across 81 native Layer 2 through Layer 7
  protocols (2,611 verified .fasm corpus scenarios) with polymorphic IPv4/IPv6 dual-stack
  flows, stateful 4-tuple TCP sequence progression, and cryptographic SNMPv3 USM
  authentication and privacy.
